Subject: [PATCH] kernel/vm: take shadowed pages out of MODIFIED before freeing them

Since 3bfaa91290 ("Per-KDiskDevice modified queues and page writers"),
which landed on 2026-07-18, a MODIFIED page's queue is found through its
cache, so vm_page_free_etc() asserts that the page is not MODIFIED: after
RemovePage() it has no cache.
That commit made VMCache::_FreePageRange() and VMCache::Delete() move such
a page to CACHED first. The two paths that free pages shadowed during an
anonymous cache merge did not:

- VMAnonymousCache::_MergePagesSmallerConsumer(), for a source page
  shadowed by a consumer page, and
- VMAnonymousCache::_MergeSwapPages(), for a source page shadowed by a
  consumer swap page.

exec() after fork() merges the area caches, and under memory pressure
sshd stopped the machine in the kernel debugger:

  PANIC: ASSERT FAILED (vm_page.cpp:3172):
    (page->State() != PAGE_STATE_MODIFIED)
  vm_page_free_etc
  VMAnonymousCache::_MergePagesSmallerConsumer
  VMCache::_MergeWithOnlyConsumer
  VMCache::Unlock
  VMCache::Delete
  delete_area
  vm_delete_areas
  _user_exec

The shadowed page's data is dropped, so it needs no write-back. Clear
"modified" and move it to CACHED while it is still in its cache, as
_FreePageRange() does.

Upstream: https://github.com/RenkuOS/Source/pull/343
Signed-off-by: rainygirl <rainygirl@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5


diff --git a/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.cpp b/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.cpp
index 0571e30b99..052d13748e 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.cpp
@@ -1232,6 +1232,21 @@ VMAnonymousCache::_SwapBlockGetAddress(off_t pageIndex)
 }
 
 
+/*static*/ void
+VMAnonymousCache::_PrepareToFreeShadowedPage(vm_page* page)
+{
+	// A page shadowed by the consumer is discarded, so it need not be written
+	// back. It must leave the MODIFIED state while it is still in its cache:
+	// a MODIFIED page's queue is found through its cache, and
+	// vm_page_free_etc() refuses one (as VMCache::_FreePageRange() and
+	// VMCache::Delete() already handle).
+	if (page->State() == PAGE_STATE_MODIFIED) {
+		page->modified = false;
+		vm_page_set_state(page, PAGE_STATE_CACHED);
+	}
+}
+
+
 void
 VMAnonymousCache::_MergePagesSmallerConsumer(VMAnonymousCache* source)
 {
@@ -1255,6 +1270,7 @@ VMAnonymousCache::_MergePagesSmallerConsumer(VMAnonymousCache* source)
 			ASSERT_PRINT(sourcePage->WiredCount() == 0
 					&& sourcePage->mappings.IsEmpty(),
 				"sourcePage: %p, page: %p", sourcePage, page);
+			_PrepareToFreeShadowedPage(sourcePage);
 			source->RemovePage(sourcePage);
 			vm_page_free_etc(source, sourcePage, &reservation);
 		}
@@ -1307,6 +1323,7 @@ VMAnonymousCache::_MergeSwapPages(VMAnonymousCache* source)
 					if (page != NULL) {
 						DEBUG_PAGE_ACCESS_START(page);
 						ASSERT_PRINT(!page->busy, "page: %p", page);
+						_PrepareToFreeShadowedPage(page);
 						source->RemovePage(page);
 						vm_page_free(source, page);
 					}
diff --git a/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.h b/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.h
index c4b8e53b96..1ed7b01adf 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.h
+++ b/src/system/kernel/vm/VMAnonymousCache.h
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@ private:
 			void				_SwapBlockFree(off_t pageIndex, uint32 count);
 			swap_addr_t			_SwapBlockGetAddress(off_t pageIndex);
 
+	static	void				_PrepareToFreeShadowedPage(vm_page* page);
 			void				_MergePagesSmallerConsumer(
 									VMAnonymousCache* source);
 			void				_MergeSwapPages(VMAnonymousCache* source);
